    "id": "thermal-mcq-346",
    "questionNumber": 346,
    "question": "Two slabs of identical cross-sectional area and equal thickness are joined in series. If their thermal conductivities are k₁ = 100 W/(m·K) and k₂ = 200 W/(m·K), what is the equivalent thermal conductivity k_eq of the composite combination?",
    "options": {
      "A": "133.33 W/(m·K)",
      "B": "150.00 W/(m·K)",
      "C": "66.67 W/(m·K)",
      "D": "600.00 W/(m·K)"
    },
    "optionsList": [
      "133.33 W/(m·K)",
      "150.00 W/(m·K)",
      "66.67 W/(m·K)",
      "600.00 W/(m·K)"
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nThermal resistances in series add directly: R_eq = R₁ + R₂. For equal thickness slabs, the equivalent thermal conductivity is the harmonic mean of the individual conductivities.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nk₁ = 100 W/(m·K), k₂ = 200 W/(m·K), L₁ = L₂ = L, Total thickness = 2L.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\n\\frac{2L}{k_{\\text{eq}} A} = \\frac{L}{k_1 A} + \\frac{L}{k_2 A} \\implies k_{\\text{eq}} = \\frac{2 k_1 k_2}{k_1 + k_2}\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Total thermal resistance: R_eq = R₁ + R₂.\n2. (2L) / (k_eq A) = (L / k₁ A) + (L / k₂ A).\n3. Canceling L/A: 2 / k_eq = (1/k₁) + (1/k₂) = (k₁ + k₂) / (k₁ k₂).\n4. Therefore, k_eq = 2 k₁ k₂ / (k₁ + k₂) = 2 × (100 × 200) / (300) = 133.33 W/(m·K).\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 133.33 W/(m·K)\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nSeries composite slabs = HARMONIC MEAN: k_eq = 2 k₁ k₂ / (k₁ + k₂). Parallel slabs = ARITHMETIC MEAN: k_eq = (k₁ + k₂) / 2.",
